cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "guarded-text2sparql: LLM-proposed SPARQL with deterministic guardrails"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Hanny
repository-code: "https://github.com/hannykumar/guarded-text2sparql"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  A text-to-SPARQL prototype over eccenca's CK25 corporate knowledge graph. A local
  language model proposes a query; deterministic guardrails (read-only, syntax,
  prefixes, vocabulary, entity existence, execution, plausibility, bounded repair)
  decide whether it is returned. Evaluated with the official TEXT2SPARQL challenge
  client, with an ablation measuring what the schema card, entity linking and the
  guardrails each contribute.
keywords:
  - text-to-SPARQL
  - knowledge graphs
  - SPARQL
  - large language models
  - guardrails
references:
  - type: data
    title: >-
      The CK25 Corporate Knowledge Reference Dataset for Benchmarking Text 2 SPARQL
      Question Answering Approaches
    authors:
      - family-names: Tramp
        given-names: Sebastian
        affiliation: eccenca GmbH
      - family-names: Pietzsch
        given-names: René
        affiliation: eccenca GmbH
    year: 2025
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.16912605
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    repository-code: "https://github.com/eccenca/ck25-dataset"
